 "signs": [
  {
   "x": 42,
   "y": 33,
   "text": "COIRE GABHAIL, the LOST VALLEY. A secret hollow between two of the Sisters, hidden from the glen below. The MacDonalds are said to have kept cattle here. A great hiding place and a very steep walk."
  },
  {
   "x": 42,
   "y": 19,
   "text": "A HIDDEN COIRE. The hill folk call a hollow like this a coire, 'a cauldron'. This one fills with mist at the drop of a hat, so tread softly. If you hear an eagle, say hello. If an eagle says hello, say it back."
  },
  {
   "x": 32,
   "y": 60,
   "text": "GLENCOE MEMORIAL. In February 1692, soldiers who had been guests of the MacDonalds turned on them. Thirty-eight people were killed, and others died fleeing into the snow. Walk gently, and stay a while."
  },
  {
   "x": 29,
   "y": 44,
   "text": "GLEANN COMHANN, GLENCOE. A glen made by ice, with sides so steep that the mist sits in the bowl like milk in a cup. Bidean nam Bian, at 1,150 m, is the highest hill in Argyll. The glen is a place to look up at."
  },
  {
   "x": 28,
   "y": 30,
   "text": "THE THREE SISTERS. Beinn Fhada, Gearr Aonach and Aonach Dubh: three great spurs of rock, shoulder to shoulder. Bond came here, and so did a boy wizard, and neither of them could get a signal."
  },
  {
   "x": 30,
   "y": 31,
   "plaque": "glencoe_ossians_cave",
   "theme": "arts",
   "title": "Ossian's Cave",
   "text": "High on the face of Aonach Dubh is a dark slit called Ossian's Cave. Legend says Ossian, the great bard of the old Gaelic tales, was born here. In the 1760s James Macpherson published 'translations' of Ossian's poems that took Europe by storm, though much of them was his own work."
  },
  {
   "x": 29,
   "y": 58,
   "plaque": "glencoe_no_campbells",
   "title": "No Hawkers or Campbells",
   "text": "The Clachaig Inn, down the glen, has long kept a sign by its door: 'No hawkers or Campbells'. It is a joke with a long memory, because the soldiers at the 1692 massacre were led by Captain Robert Campbell of Glenlyon. Campbells are, in fact, served. Usually."
  }
 ],
